"Let $f(n)$ denote the minimum possible length of the shortest cycle in a tournament on $n$ vertices. **Asymptotic shortest-cycle conjecture.** For all $n\\ge 4$,\n\n$$\nf(n)=\\left(\\frac{1}{3}+o(1)\\right)n^2.\n$$\n\nThis is the asymptotic form of the claim that the paper's construction is best possible: the available bounds give the matching leading constant, while the exact value remains unresolved in general."